        "temperament": "Relaxed",
        "wild": "Helicoprion frendo is an ancient shark-like fish with a distinctive spiral tooth whorl in its lower jaw. Despite its fearsome appearance, it is surprisingly relaxed in temperament and does not actively hunt survivors unless provoked. It seems content to cruise through ocean waters, feeding on soft-bodied creatures like jellyfish and squid.",
